      "ref": "Avodah Zarah 7a:8",
      "english": "<strong>The Sages taught:</strong> A person may not say to another on Shabbat: <b>Does it seem that you will join me this evening?</b> This is prohibited, as the speaker is hinting that he would like to hire the person being spoken to for labor after the conclusion of Shabbat. <b>Rabbi Yehoshua ben Korḥa says:</b> A person may say to another on Shabbat: <b>Does it seem that you will join me this evening?</b> In this case, he is not asking the person explicitly. <b>Rabba bar bar Ḥana says</b> that <b>Rabbi Yoḥanan says: The <i>halakha</i></b> is <b>in accordance with</b> the opinion of <b>Rabbi Yehoshua ben Korḥa.</b>"
    },
